`medium` also passes the full six-attack panel at 0/8, including the two-million-node exact maximal-biclique DPLL. I have therefore set `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY = "medium"` and updated the certificate bounds. The earlier G9 runs targeted the old `hard` preset, so I’m rerunning both diagnostics at the actual shipping preset; they are independent and can run concurrently.
exec
/bin/bash -lc '(
  cd g9_hinted_run
  GV_HINT_MODE=structural python3 ../../../scripts/harden.py gen_2010_05733.py
) &
hinted_pid=$!
(
  cd g9_placebo_run
  GV_HINT_MODE=placebo python3 ../../../scripts/harden.py gen_2010_05733.py
) &
placebo_pid=$!
wait "$hinted_pid"
hinted_status=$?
wait "$placebo_pid"
placebo_status=$?
echo "hinted_status=$hinted_status placebo_status=$placebo_status"' in /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.05733
