Completed a verified Track A generator based on Section 4, Lemma 6 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.05733).

- [gen_2010_05733.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.05733/gen_2010_05733.py) — inverse-generated maximal-biclique certificates carried into VC-\((k+4)\) graph square roots.
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.05733/selftest_report.json) — all G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.05733/README.md) — construction, theorem regime, worked demo, measurements, and caveats.
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.05733/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl) — `easy` solved 1/3; shipping preset `medium` hardened 0/3.
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.05733/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl) and [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2010.05733/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl) — both 0/3 at shipping size.

Key measurements: 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses, all six attacks 0/8, exact DPLL exhausted 2,000,000 nodes on every shipping instance, and the answer is 806 characters with 26 atomic elements. Some oracle failures were response-budget exhaustion rather than incorrect completed answers; this is documented in the README.
